# Build context filter for the master image (infra/docker/master.Dockerfile),
# whose context is the repository root.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: without it every `docker build` at the repo root ships the
# entire Ironfront_Reborn Unity project (gigabytes of Library/, imported assets and a
# TerrainData asset) plus any local .env, backups, TLS material and Terraform state to
# the daemon. That is slow, and it is how a secret ends up baked into an image layer.
# The master build needs only the root MSBuild props, global.json and the three .NET
# projects in its reference graph — everything else is excluded.
#
# The game-server image builds from a DIFFERENT context (the Unity Linux artifact dir,
# e.g. build/server) and is unaffected by this file.

# Version control and editor/tooling state.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vs
.vscode
.idea
.claude
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# .NET build outputs — regenerated inside the image; stale local copies must not leak in.
**/bin
**/obj
**/*.binlog

# The Unity project: enormous and not part of the master's build graph.
Ironfront_Reborn/

# Unity dedicated-server artifacts and generic build output.
build/
builds/

# Everything that is not the master's source or build contract.
infra/
docs/
plans/
tools/
**/*.md

# Secrets and runtime state — must NEVER enter an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.crt
backups/
tls/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.log
**/*.csv
